  "description": "T1 Sycamore (Acer pseudoplatanus)\rCarry out a crown reduction of the Sycamore, reducing the overall canopy by approximately 1.5 metres back to suitable growth points throughout the crown.\rWorks shall be undertaken selectively to maintain the tree's natural form, balance and healthy furnishing growth whilst improving light penetration to the adjacent property and garden. All pruning cuts shall be made to appropriate secondary growth points in accordance with BS39982010 - Tree Work Recommendations.  All timber, brash and associated arisings shall be removed from site and disposed of responsibly. Upon completion, the work area shall be left clean and tidy.\r\rT2 Cherry (Prunus sp.)\rReduce the height of the Cherry tree by approximately 1.0 metre and reduce the lateral spread by approximately 2.0 metres, pruning back to suitable growth points throughout the crown.  Works shall be undertaken selectively to improve light penetration into the adjacent property and garden whilst maintaining the tree's natural form, balance and healthy furnishing growth. All pruning cuts shall be made to appropriate secondary growth points in accordance with BS39982010 - Tree Work Recommendations.\r\r\rReason for works:\r\rGeneral tree maintenance",
